WEBVTT


00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:59.148
-Hey, babe, it's me.
- Hey, baby doll.


00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:01.157
Yeah, I'm in the car already.
Are you on your way?


00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:03.353
Yep, I'm almost there.


00:01:03.496 --> 00:01:04.793
OK. I'll see you soon.


00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:06.728
- I love you, babe.
- I love you too.


00:01:09.703 --> 00:01:12.399
Out of the fuckin' car, bitch! Now!


00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:13.761
Shane?


00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:15.797
Shane!


00:01:21.448 --> 00:01:22.881
You OK?


00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:28.181
- Come back, I'm gonna kill you, bitch!
- No! Shane? Don't leave me!


00:01:33.182 --> 00:01:38.982
Subtitles: Arigon


00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:08.653
You hunted him down,


00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:11.696
just like you used to hunt down
the enemy on the battlefield.


00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:14.391
You're a trained killer who went
after the stupid son of a bitch


00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:16.434
who went after your wife! Admit it!


00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:19.994
Shane!


00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:23.238
I don't know what you're talking about.
You got the wrong man.


00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:26.573
That's bullshit. We checked your past.


00:02:26.713 --> 00:02:32.618
You were Special Forces.
Someone took this guy apart!


00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:39.587
Look at you. Now you're just a murderer.
What the hell happened to you?


00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:42.217
The guy carjacked my wife.
I chased him off.


00:02:42.362 --> 00:02:44.159
It doesn't mean I killed him.


00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:53.865
You're going away
for a long time, tough guy.


00:03:59.105 --> 00:04:02.370
- Yeah, where he's at.
- Come on, bitch!


00:04:09.616 --> 00:04:11.550
Yo, what's up, man?


00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:35.337
I'm sorry, so very sorry.


00:04:35.475 --> 00:04:38.672
I know I promised to wait for you,
but I can't wait any longer.


00:04:38.812 --> 00:04:41.110
It's been 6 years, I need to move on.


00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:43.175
I need to get my life back.


00:04:49.289 --> 00:04:51.086
I love you so much, Shane.


00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:11.075
Get out of here, Daniels!
Big day's tomorrow.


00:05:22.856 --> 00:05:24.414
Counsel, I take it that you're ready?


00:05:24.991 --> 00:05:28.722
We are, Your Honor. I believe you have
our recommendation in front of you?


00:05:28.862 --> 00:05:32.025
As you've read, the prosecution
has filed for a dismissal of charges


00:05:32.165 --> 00:05:36.295
against my client, and, because of that,
we will expect certain details


00:05:36.436 --> 00:05:39.667
to be included in the record
when his record is expunged.


00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:42.067
And what are those?


00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:45.041
That a weapon,
one that matches the ballistics profile


00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:47.112
of the one used in the initial murder,


00:05:47.247 --> 00:05:50.614
was recovered in the possession
of another subject.


00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:55.585
That the DNA of said subject
matches the DNA that was recovered


00:05:55.722 --> 00:05:58.520
in the initial murder investigation.


00:05:58.658 --> 00:06:03.357
All of this was brought to light
with the help of Project Innocence.


00:06:06.332 --> 00:06:08.800
And that DNA was never admitted
into the original trial?


00:06:12.906 --> 00:06:18.105
OK. I find sufficient evidence
to support a dismissal


00:06:18.244 --> 00:06:20.712
of any and all charges
against the defendant.


00:06:21.114 --> 00:06:25.380
Also, the state will award
Mr. Daniels $300,000,


00:06:26.019 --> 00:06:31.457
$50,000 for each year Mr. Daniels
was erroneously incarcerated.


00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:34.583
I trust you are satisfied with that,
Mr. Daniels?


00:06:37.764 --> 00:06:41.632
Your Honor, I gave 14 years
of my life to the military,


00:06:41.768 --> 00:06:44.931
6 years hard time
in a federal penitentiary.


00:06:46.506 --> 00:06:51.068
I don't know why you people think
that money can replace a life.


00:06:54.681 --> 00:06:59.414
There are no words to describe
what it's like when you're


00:06:59.552 --> 00:07:04.353
an innocent man in prison, sitting there
and waiting and hoping and praying


00:07:04.490 --> 00:07:06.583
that this day will come.


00:07:06.726 --> 00:07:10.662
I don't believe that money can buy back


00:07:10.797 --> 00:07:14.927
my name, my reputation,


00:07:15.068 --> 00:07:19.505
my wife, my family, and all that I lost.


00:07:19.639 --> 00:07:23.632
Mr. Daniels,
the court recognizes your grief


00:07:23.776 --> 00:07:26.074
and we sympathize with your loss...


00:07:26.212 --> 00:07:30.114
I don't want your money.
I want my life back.


00:09:00.306 --> 00:09:02.103
Take him to the safe house.


00:09:09.482 --> 00:09:11.746
A nice lady like you
needs a nice car like this.


00:09:11.884 --> 00:09:13.943
Come on, I'll take you for a ride.


00:09:14.087 --> 00:09:15.076
Come on, get in.


00:09:15.221 --> 00:09:17.849
This car's worth more than you
can trade. Look here, it's a great deal.


00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.617
Tonight, right now. Get in.


00:10:08.441 --> 00:10:11.001
You should shut your mouth
for one fuckin' second and listen.


00:10:11.144 --> 00:10:12.873
That's why you're slippin', dawg.


00:10:13.613 --> 00:10:17.481
Yo. Want to buy some wheels?


00:10:17.617 --> 00:10:19.482
Naw, man, you know...
I don't know, how much?


00:10:19.619 --> 00:10:21.917
How much? For this classic car?


00:10:22.789 --> 00:10:25.383
Tell you what:
I like your face, so...


00:10:25.525 --> 00:10:27.322
- How about everything you got?
- Everything I've got?


00:10:27.460 --> 00:10:28.927
Look, man, you want to jack me?
Is that it?


00:10:29.061 --> 00:10:30.961
- Yeah, that's it.
- Let me tell you something.


00:10:31.097 --> 00:10:33.895
I just got out of prison for something
I didn't do, and, before that,


00:10:34.033 --> 00:10:36.593
I used to, like, you know,
study real hard


00:10:36.736 --> 00:10:40.866
and learned all kinds of different ways
to kill motherfuckers just like you.


00:10:41.007 --> 00:10:42.668
This motherfucker talking shit.


00:10:42.809 --> 00:10:47.837
So let me go. Just let me go on by,
or I'll fuck you up ugly.


00:10:50.016 --> 00:10:51.984
- "Fuck you up ugly," he says.
- Both of us?


00:10:52.118 --> 00:10:54.109
Tell me something.
What's that mean, "Fuck you up ugly?"


00:10:54.253 --> 00:10:57.347
It means your mama
won't recognize you in your coffin.


00:10:57.490 --> 00:11:00.516
Talking about my mama?
Hand it over, motherfucker.


00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:12.060
See this gun here?


00:11:12.205 --> 00:11:15.368
I'm just gonna pop the slide release,
then pull this bitch off...


00:11:16.242 --> 00:11:19.405
and then I'm gonna take this
and I'm gonna fuck you up ugly.


00:11:19.545 --> 00:11:21.206
No! No, no!


00:11:32.592 --> 00:11:34.321
Fuck you.


00:11:54.247 --> 00:11:56.841
Put that shit away, boy,
before somebody gets hurt.


00:12:03.656 --> 00:12:07.057
Now count to 100,
and get some help for those 2 fools.


00:12:18.337 --> 00:12:20.532
- I'm taking this car, bitch.
- Bring it, motherfucker.


00:12:27.713 --> 00:12:30.580
20, 21, 22...


00:12:56.576 --> 00:12:58.134
What is this shit?


00:12:59.712 --> 00:13:01.043
Come on.


00:13:04.216 --> 00:13:06.514
OK, just pick a station, man.
My ears are throwing up.


00:13:06.652 --> 00:13:09.621
Just relax, man.
I'm just trying to find a good station.


00:13:09.755 --> 00:13:11.382
Listen to DJ, man.


00:13:12.291 --> 00:13:15.556
Look, I gotta take a leak, Sergey.
Pull over, man.


00:13:15.695 --> 00:13:16.889
- Are you serious?
- I'm serious.


00:13:17.496 --> 00:13:20.397
Man... You've always
gotta take a squirt, man.


00:13:22.068 --> 00:13:25.037
- Dude, slow down, man. That was a cop.
- Yeah. Yeah, I saw him.


00:13:25.171 --> 00:13:27.969
Man, you better throw that out.
We got an open container issue here.


00:13:28.507 --> 00:13:31.999
Open con...
We got a stolen car issue here, man.


00:13:32.144 --> 00:13:34.044
I hope they did a good job on the VIN.


00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:36.478
That's true. He's probably
hammering a donut, anyway.


00:13:36.616 --> 00:13:38.345
He didn't even look up when we passed.


00:13:39.218 --> 00:13:42.085
Let me toss the rest of the empties out
when we get to the rest stop, all right?


00:13:42.788 --> 00:13:45.313
- Yeah.
- I gotta take a squirt. Come on.


00:13:46.492 --> 00:13:49.086
Just pull over, man!
There's a rest stop ahead.


00:13:49.228 --> 00:13:51.696
Take a right. Take a right here.


00:14:00.139 --> 00:14:01.663
I love you so much, Shane.


00:14:59.899 --> 00:15:04.336
I'm sure!
Well, we won't talk, we won't talk.


00:15:08.641 --> 00:15:10.871
No problem. Got that for you.


00:15:13.079 --> 00:15:14.910
- You should go pee.
- That's what I'm gonna do.


00:15:15.047 --> 00:15:18.210
- Go put those in a can.
- Yeah, I'll do that.


00:15:22.121 --> 00:15:26.217
Damn. You're luck... lucky
I don't throw the glass one at you!


00:15:46.112 --> 00:15:49.809
We have a 629, 2 males down,
liquor store on Hastings.


00:15:49.949 --> 00:15:51.473
Unit 5, please respond.


00:15:51.617 --> 00:15:55.018
Potential suspects in black 300.
Will approach.


00:16:20.146 --> 00:16:22.171
Driver's license and registration?


00:16:25.384 --> 00:16:26.749
No English. Sorry.


00:16:29.088 --> 00:16:30.817
You? You speak English?


00:16:35.528 --> 00:16:36.790
OK, get out.


00:16:45.104 --> 00:16:47.038
Put your hands on the car.


00:16:47.606 --> 00:16:50.666
Drop your keys
and put your hands on the car.


00:17:10.563 --> 00:17:11.552
Step off to the side.


00:17:12.865 --> 00:17:14.958
Take a step to the side.


00:17:18.771 --> 00:17:19.965
Whose car?


00:17:24.677 --> 00:17:26.235
What's in the trunk?


00:17:26.378 --> 00:17:27.868
You don't understand?


00:17:28.013 --> 00:17:30.709
You can't tell me whose car it is
or what's in the trunk?


00:17:38.724 --> 00:17:40.055
What's this?


00:17:40.793 --> 00:17:42.021
Shirt.


00:17:42.161 --> 00:17:44.322
Shirt? What, clothes?


00:17:49.034 --> 00:17:51.025
Wanna hurry, before that cop
decides to mess with us, too?


00:17:51.170 --> 00:17:52.398
Coming.


00:18:11.724 --> 00:18:13.191
Fuck.


00:18:14.460 --> 00:18:17.258
Please... just go. Take the car and go.


00:18:17.496 --> 00:18:19.930
Can't do that, man.
You'd call back up.


00:18:20.065 --> 00:18:22.056
Here, take my radio.


00:18:24.870 --> 00:18:25.962
Take my radio!


00:18:27.373 --> 00:18:30.103
- Holy shit!
- Please! Please...


00:18:30.242 --> 00:18:31.368
Shit!


00:18:35.114 --> 00:18:36.979
- Run, man!
- Markov!


00:18:57.169 --> 00:18:59.160
- Please...
- Who's in charge now?


00:19:21.660 --> 00:19:23.821
Come on! Come on, buddy!


00:19:30.836 --> 00:19:31.825
Come on!


00:20:12.511 --> 00:20:13.705
Shoot this motherfucker!


00:21:11.236 --> 00:21:12.794
What the hell? Hey.


00:21:12.938 --> 00:21:14.872
Take it easy. I'm the good guy.


00:21:15.007 --> 00:21:17.635
You're just in the wrong place
at the wrong time.


00:21:29.855 --> 00:21:32.722
Man. Shitload of cash in here.
Did you know that?


00:21:33.859 --> 00:21:35.019
What do you want to do now?


00:21:35.160 --> 00:21:38.459
- Is that car of yours drivable?
- Yeah, more or less.


00:21:38.597 --> 00:21:39.655
Go start it up.


00:21:42.267 --> 00:21:46.601
Holy fuck! There's a body in here, man.
Get the car started now.


00:21:48.507 --> 00:21:49.940
Now!


00:22:01.753 --> 00:22:04.586
Who's this? Is she dead?


00:22:04.723 --> 00:22:05.815
No.


00:22:12.898 --> 00:22:14.195
Hurry! We've got company!


00:22:15.868 --> 00:22:16.857
OK, go.


00:22:25.010 --> 00:22:25.999
Fuck.


00:23:14.459 --> 00:23:15.790
What's your name?


00:23:19.464 --> 00:23:20.453
Tia.


00:23:31.343 --> 00:23:32.401
Where am I?


00:23:32.544 --> 00:23:34.535
We're just going up the road.


00:23:35.514 --> 00:23:37.880
We found you in the trunk of a car.


00:23:40.852 --> 00:23:42.080
What?


00:23:44.656 --> 00:23:47.955
I was... I was with my friends.


00:23:55.067 --> 00:23:56.728
What about all that cash?


00:23:59.805 --> 00:24:00.965
I don't know.


00:24:05.010 --> 00:24:06.272
I went to a meeting...


00:24:12.784 --> 00:24:15.719
...with a man
about an immigration issue.


00:24:22.361 --> 00:24:26.957
Take it easy. You've been drugged.
It'll probably wear off soon.


00:24:27.099 --> 00:24:28.293
My fr...


00:24:35.107 --> 00:24:36.597
My friends...


00:24:42.214 --> 00:24:44.580
I think... I think they...


00:24:44.716 --> 00:24:46.479
I think...


00:24:46.618 --> 00:24:48.483
I think they killed them.


00:24:51.723 --> 00:24:53.156
She's out again.


00:24:55.060 --> 00:24:56.994
Look, do you have any idea
what's going on here?


00:24:57.129 --> 00:25:00.530
Just get us to the next town. That sign
back there says Bellingham in 50.


00:25:00.666 --> 00:25:02.099
Well, I live in East Bellingham.


00:25:02.234 --> 00:25:04.566
What the hell do I tell the cops
if I'm stopped?


00:25:04.703 --> 00:25:07.228
Do you have any idea who these people
were that were shooting at us?


00:25:07.372 --> 00:25:09.067
I mean, for that matter, who are you?


00:25:09.574 --> 00:25:11.633
I don't think it really matters anymore.


00:25:11.943 --> 00:25:14.707
After you drop me off,
just tell the cops whatever you want.


00:25:15.213 --> 00:25:17.613
Just give me a few hours
to get into the wind.


00:25:18.417 --> 00:25:20.647
Well, my father'd disown me
if I spoke to the cops,


00:25:20.786 --> 00:25:22.151
especially the ones from Bellingham.


00:25:22.487 --> 00:25:26.048
Is your father a gangster or something?
Ex-con?


00:25:26.191 --> 00:25:29.820
Well, it's like I said, my father's
not exactly an upstanding citizen.


00:25:29.961 --> 00:25:33.124
He sells cars that aren't necessarily
for sale, if you know what I mean.


00:25:33.265 --> 00:25:34.755
I could relate to that.


00:26:01.293 --> 00:26:03.989
Hey. Welcome back.


00:26:06.031 --> 00:26:09.694
I wouldn't do that if I were you.
We're going about 70 miles an hour.


00:26:10.902 --> 00:26:15.566
It's OK. We saved you from those guys
back there. We don't mean you any harm.


00:26:15.707 --> 00:26:17.641
What do you mean "we", white boy?


00:26:17.776 --> 00:26:21.075
OK, technically, he did.
I did drive the car, though.


00:26:21.213 --> 00:26:23.272
Are you going with him?
Is she going with you?


00:26:23.415 --> 00:26:26.816
My advice is just drop her off
at the first cop-shop.


00:26:26.952 --> 00:26:31.013
- No. I can't go to the local police.
- No? Why's that?


00:26:31.323 --> 00:26:32.950
They're the ones who killed my friends.


00:26:33.091 --> 00:26:36.390
- Damn.
- Look, I need to call my father.


00:26:36.528 --> 00:26:39.292
Not until we reach Bellingham, then
you're free to do whatever you want.


00:26:39.431 --> 00:26:43.925
But I need help. Didn't you hear me?
The cops killed my friends.


00:26:48.306 --> 00:26:50.638
My father will pay you if you help me.


00:26:50.776 --> 00:26:54.542
The problem is, I don't need any money.
Got a whole bag of cash here.


00:26:59.317 --> 00:27:01.945
Maybe instead of money, your dad
can get me the fuck out of America?


00:27:02.087 --> 00:27:04.612
- Could he do that?
- He can.


00:27:04.923 --> 00:27:08.723
Yeah? Well, if you're so sure
about that, I'll tell you what, son.


00:27:08.860 --> 00:27:11.852
Drop her and I off together,
and then you park this piece of shit


00:27:11.997 --> 00:27:15.990
somewhere where nobody can see it
and hightail it to the fuckin' moon.


00:27:16.134 --> 00:27:19.797
Maybe I can help. I know the town
really well. My father's got connections.


00:27:19.938 --> 00:27:23.271
Just forget about us, man.
Do what I said.


00:28:01.246 --> 00:28:03.043
- Hey.
- Let's see what we got.


00:28:18.463 --> 00:28:19.623
Nice.


00:29:02.207 --> 00:29:03.606
Now you're a hero.


00:29:04.910 --> 00:29:07.902
Lay that dead kid so it looks like
the chink killed him first.


00:29:08.046 --> 00:29:11.174
I want this whole thing tied up
by the time the state boys get here.


00:29:11.316 --> 00:29:14.080
- You got it. Let's go.
- Yeah, OK.


00:29:33.204 --> 00:29:34.796
Pull up over here, kid.


00:29:47.752 --> 00:29:50.118
All right, listen.
You're gonna get out here.


00:29:50.255 --> 00:29:52.655
Put as much distance as you can
between yourself and the car.


00:29:52.791 --> 00:29:54.554
These guys
are gonna come looking for you.


00:29:54.693 --> 00:29:56.285
They're gonna come looking hard,
you hear?


00:29:56.428 --> 00:29:58.589
I'll wipe it down.
They'll never trace it back to me.


00:29:59.297 --> 00:30:00.286
Thank you.


00:30:02.300 --> 00:30:04.598
Look, if you guys ever need anything,
you go to Little Russia,


00:30:04.736 --> 00:30:06.897
you ask for Vlad. That's my father.


00:30:07.038 --> 00:30:08.232
He does some other business, too.


00:30:10.809 --> 00:30:12.640
All right, man, be safe.


00:30:15.680 --> 00:30:17.272
Thanks.


00:30:24.289 --> 00:30:27.258
- Where you going?
- I thought we were...


00:30:27.392 --> 00:30:29.917
Yeah, no, we're not going there.
Come on.


00:30:32.931 --> 00:30:34.922
Wait. Wait for me.


00:30:37.168 --> 00:30:38.829
Here? Why?


00:30:38.970 --> 00:30:40.597
They catch that kid and we're fucked,
and from him,


00:30:40.739 --> 00:30:42.798
they'll roll back to that other motel.
You understand?


00:30:42.941 --> 00:30:44.772
You don't trust anyone, do you?


00:30:44.909 --> 00:30:47.469
It ain't about trust,
it's about survival.


00:30:58.590 --> 00:31:00.922
Look, I need to call my father.


00:31:01.860 --> 00:31:03.418
I need to tell him I'm OK.


00:31:03.561 --> 00:31:07.964
Before you do that, I think you
and I need to have a little talk.


00:31:09.367 --> 00:31:12.200
I already told you everything.
What more do you want me to say?


00:31:12.337 --> 00:31:15.932
You told me that your friends
were killed by local cops.


00:31:16.074 --> 00:31:18.406
That really doesn't explain to me
how you ended up in a trunk


00:31:18.543 --> 00:31:19.976
next to a bag of cash.


00:31:20.111 --> 00:31:22.443
I already told you, it's not my money.
What are you, deaf?


00:31:22.580 --> 00:31:24.013
I want you to shut the fuck up.


00:31:24.249 --> 00:31:27.150
I want you to pay attention
and understand one thing.


00:31:27.285 --> 00:31:30.584
If I'm gonna try to save you,
and if I'm gonna try to help you,


00:31:30.722 --> 00:31:33.987
you need to talk to me, you need to
listen to what I say, when I say,


00:31:34.125 --> 00:31:36.491
how I say, and if you don't,
I will leave you here


00:31:36.628 --> 00:31:40.564
to get eaten by the fuckin' jackals,
who are coming soon.


00:31:42.467 --> 00:31:43.764
OK?


00:31:45.070 --> 00:31:47.561
OK. I'm sorry.


00:31:47.706 --> 00:31:51.233
If you want me to help you,
you gotta talk to me, man.


00:31:51.376 --> 00:31:55.472
You gotta tell me straight,
so I can know who's coming for us.


00:31:55.613 --> 00:31:58.946
You're right. You saved my life.


